### Limitations the authors admit
- 2019A&A...625A.118K: Hydro models assume vertically isothermal disk; delta v_rot may be underestimated
- 2019A&A...625A.118K: Beam smearing and limited spectral resolution complicate rotation-curve interpretation
- 2019ApJ...871..100H: Offset smaller than beam; calibration issue or proper motion not excluded
- 2020ApJ...895L...2N: Masses highly uncertain due to cm dust opacity
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Short snapshot observations, lack of short spacings, gas radii as lower limits
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Dust masses are lower limits if optically thick
- 2024ApJ...969..143I: Cosmic ray ionization estimate uncertain by order of magnitude; N(H2CO) poorly constrained
- 2016A&A...593L..19M: Non-simultaneous spectrum assuming no variability; sparse sub-GHz coverage.
- 2026ApJ..1004..126K: Spectral shape uncertain with narrow frequency range and large errors
- 2018ApJ...857...19F: Missed flux relative to APEX (median 63% recovered), possibly low surface brightness emission
- 2018ApJ...857...19F: Sampled range of environments limited to inner rising rotation curve
- 2019ApJ...884L..58U: Non-simultaneous multi-wavelength polarimetry limits conclusions
- 2020ApJ...891...48H: Temperature, flux calibration and degeneracies prevent precise grain size measurements
- 2020A&A...642A..96P: Limits are less constraining than the 4-8 GHz limits given the expected spectral index; only a single few-hour epoch.
- 2016A&A...593A..44L: Absolute flux uncertain (~20%) because Titan scans were largely flagged; single epoch only.
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: Calibration uncertainty not included in fit uncertainties; line flux scaling anomalies in some tunings
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: STATCONT continuum subtraction not optimal for lines near noise level
- 2016A&A...594A.107K: ALMA observations have 1-2 arcsec offsets from ICRS and were not designed for astrometry
- 2016A&A...594A.107K: S-star proper motions not statistically significant; nature of S stars poorly constrained by broadband photometry
- 2023NatAs...7...80U: PA difference between radio and optical only ~90% significant
- 2026ApJ..1003L..17Y: Fit decay timescales are approximate because of limited light-curve duration
- 2025ApJ...987..152R: 86-100 GHz results inconclusive
- 2015ApJ...805..186L: Southern jet not continuous beyond ~10 arcsec, so point symmetry unconfirmed
- 2020A&A...636A..62K: Photon index uncertainties too large for quantitative analysis
- 2024AJ....167...94H: Clump B Doppler velocity very uncertain
- 2024AJ....167...94H: Mass lower bounds for C and D; clumps poorly resolved
- 2014ApJ...791...20R: Sample biased toward brightest disks; dust opacity absolute values unconstrained
- 2018MNRAS.479.5440L: Velocity map very uncertain due to beam smearing and low S/N; Sigma not robust
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: LVG parameters highly degenerate; best-fit values reflect relative trends only
- 2020A&A...641A.155V: Sample biased to upper main sequence and warm dust by PACS detection requirement
- 2017MNRAS.469.4726N: Short-spacing correction crude and unreliable
- 2019ApJ...881...33H: Short observations may miss flares; emission mechanism cannot be inferred from non-detections
- 2021A&A...652A..92N: Observed p-mode rms is a lower limit since resolution is coarse and pixels are correlated
- 2015A&A...576A..41B: Results from a single track; ALMA cadence coarse
- 2016RAA....16..111N: Model is crude; uncertainties are not reliable quantitatively
- 2016RAA....16..111N: Data cannot separate gas density and temperature
- 2015ApJ...798..124R: Data cannot distinguish between gap and double power-law forms; dust opacity degenerate with surface density
- 2024ApJ...970...56P: VLA bands observed sequentially, not simultaneously, so no instantaneous spectrum.
- 2024RMxAA..60..355R: ALMA flux lower than Faramaz et al. because ACA data were not included
- 2015ApJ...802...69B: ALMA lacked Tsys measurements on Sgr A* itself, requiring a correction
- 2017ApJ...846L..26W: Single optically thick CO line likely underestimates gas mass
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Tex is poorly constrained because data points are scattered at low S/N; may be underestimated by factor ~2
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Disk is optically thick in dust so molecules near the midplane cannot be probed
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Single excitation temperature is a large source of uncertainty.
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Spectral index poorly constrained because bands 6 and 7 are adjacent; fluxes and globule mass are lower bounds.
- 2024ApJ...976..132H: FUV fields are upper bounds from projected separations; temperature uncertainty dominates dust-trap and planet-mass estimates; SVI is approximate
- 2024A&A...690A..46S: Observations not designed for outflows; large-scale emission filtered, parameters are lower limits
- 2024ApJ...966...51G: LTE assumptions, possibly optically thin 12CO; sensitivity limited to several Msun/pc^2
- 2024ApJ...966...51G: 8um may trace gas column rather than star formation at these scales
- 2019PASJ...71...68K: Nucleus distance is hard to determine due to line of sight
- 2019PASJ...71...68K: CO(3-2) shows negative signals from sparse uv coverage
- 2017ApJ...850L..21K: Degeneracy due to few detections and large Epeak uncertainty
- 2020ApJ...892..111F: Sensitivity non-uniform so occurrence is likely underestimated; sample biased toward large bright disks
- 2019ApJ...872....2R: Second epoch used only for detection check because of poor data quality; densities are lower limits
- 2020ApJ...895..135K: Anti-correlation is tentative; H2 dissociation conflicts with Spitzer-based H2 surface density of Rosario+19; follow-up observations needed
- 2025ApJ...994..256Y: Model neglects GR effects and finite hotspot size in the fit; uncertainties are statistical only; hotspot temporal changes not modelled; spin unconstrained
- 2025MNRAS.540..364A: Sparse simultaneous multiwavelength data prevent detailed study of the double flare
- 2014PASJ...66..106H: Model assumes a saturated maser and collisional pumping only, with superseded collision rates
- 2017ApJ...844..158S: Cloud contamination limits CO and CN usability; Teff uncertainties limit comparison
- 2018A&A...619A..40M: Only one epoch; limited frequency coverage; no nutation; simple model
- 2020ApJ...889..178B: Largest uncertainty is the poorly constrained mass of Src x
- 2024ApJ...971..129C: Only two bands constrain four parameters; priors needed; porosity unconstrained
- 2024ApJ...961..108K: Inclination, Tex, stellar R, M, f_acc are uncertain; mass accretion rate varies by factor 45
- 2016A&A...586A..70L: Irregular, sparse time sampling prevents robust variability analysis; VI are lower limits.
- 2024ApJ...976...88L: Literature comparison sample is heterogeneous and of differing data quality
- 2017A&A...602A..42K: 22 GHz line uncertain due to NH3 contamination; same dilution factor assumed for all lines
- 2019ApJ...878L..26L: Systematic uncertainties from RS dynamics approximations and stochastic random walk; forward-shock parameters degenerate since nu_a not located
- 2020A&A...635L...9P: SE arm only marginally reproduced by the model
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: gamma Vir models lack constraints at other wavelengths; temperature minimum cannot be analyzed
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: Variability at longer timescales cannot be ruled out for gamma Lep
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Formal errors on fit parameters likely underestimated
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Dust mass uncertainties ignore temperature and optical depth
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Model fails to reproduce amplitude of azimuthal asymmetries
- 2017SciA....3E2935L: Mass estimate highly uncertain; model is illustrative and lacks self-consistent temperature and scattering
- 2021ApJ...908..175C: Complex maser distributions in MM1-W1 and UCHII-W1 may affect proper motions
- 2025ApJ...984L..15P: Classification is subjective and inclination-biased
- 2025ApJ...984L..15P: Vertically isothermal assumption is a major limitation
- 2025ApJ...993..120H: Dust mass may be a lower limit if emission is optically thick
- 2025ApJ...993..120H: A closer unresolved binary cannot be ruled out
- 2019ApJ...883L...2M: For PKS 1510-089 the minimum may be a low state of the core matching IC/CMB by chance.
- 2017ApJ...841...43E: Mass ratios are not true efficiencies as the association of complex with cloud is unknown
- 2018ApJ...862...94L: nu_a not constrained, causing parameter degeneracies; epsilon_e~0.9 problematic
- 2019ApJ...871....5T: The ring width is comparable to the beam, so the estimates are tentative; the model is not a full fit and the HCO+ pattern is not reproduced.
- 2018ApJ...854...56L: Disk model is illustrative only, from single frequency
- 2025ApJ...993...85Y: Ring clumps only 3-5 sigma; higher SNR needed to confirm the SW clump
- 2025ApJ...993...85Y: Low spectral index evidence tentative
- 2024ApJ...964...48T: Simulation cannot be quantitatively compared; observations only sensitive to timescales longer than ~5 yr
- 2018ApJ...868..101B: Largest fitted RMs are suspect due to phase wrap, poor fits and calibration errors at low polarization
- 2018ApJ...868..113T: Resolution (~29 au) leaves velocity features unresolved, underestimating depth
- 2018ApJ...868..113T: Cannot disentangle pressure gradient from stellar mass; pressure scaling depends on assumed density
- 2019ApJ...874...31W: Axisymmetric model cannot represent asymmetric knot B6; knot B7 not reproduced
- 2021ApJ...906...16S: Poor sampling of 10-100 GHz and limited variability data
- 2019ApJ...877L..22L: Dominant errors are systematic from opacity uncertainties and not assessed; poor MCMC convergence outside ±10 AU and at center
- 2018ApJ...859..165S: Model is simple, axisymmetric, excludes rotation, matched by eye; short spacings missing to trace hourglass
- 2018ApJ...856..117F: Mock tests recover temperature poorly (20-50%) far from the tau=1 surface
- 2018ApJ...856..117F: Source of discrepancy not conclusively identified
- 2019ApJ...871...72M: True flare timescale unknown; no simultaneous data at other wavelengths; no polarimetry
- 2018ApJ...869L..42H: Width and depth definitions ignore beam effects; narrow features are bounds
- 2018ApJ...869L..42H: Selection bias toward bright, large disks
- 2019ApJ...870...59S: Combining whole-band data is less robust owing to beam changes and interpolation
- 2019ApJ...878L...8T: Millimeter data alone cannot determine whether a planet exists; CPD may not fully account for the flux
- 2018ApJ...866...87B: CS line emission not modelled because Band 10 data scales do not match
- 2017ApJ...843..150F: Parametric temperature/density structure, degeneracies with abundance, dust-to-gas ratio and 18O abundance; turbulence is a disk-averaged intensity-weighted value
- 2018ApJ...869L..43H: Pitch angles uncertain because ring substructures or spurs complicate analysis
- 2017ApJ...840...32T: Missing flux on scales >2.1" affects spiral morphology and contrast

