### 2024AJ....167...94H: The Hidden Clumps in VY CMa Uncovered by the Atacama Large Millimeter/submillimeter Array (2024; evolved_stars; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the motions, orientations, masses and ejection times of the four ALMA clumps near VY CMa, and what do the CO maps reveal about the outer ejecta?
- step 1: Measure clump proper motions
  - method: Simultaneous 2D Gaussian fits to five continuum peaks in 2015 and 2021 images, compare offsets from VY CMa [The Fitting Method for the Proper Motio…: "2D Gaussian compoments were then fit to all five peaks simultaneously"]
  - software: CASA imfit
  - parameter: Position errors approx (synthesised beam)/(S/N) [The Fitting Method for the Proper Motio…: "approximately (synthesised beam)/(S/N), for moderately extended array configurations (ALMA memo 620)"]
  - assumption: Distance 1.15 kpc [Proper Motions of the Clumps: "at a distance of 1.15 kpc"]
  - validation: Residual images after subtraction have rms 0.4 and 0.2 mJy (2015, 2021) [The Fitting Method for the Proper Motio…: "the residual images have rms 0.4 and 0.2 mJy for the 2015 and 2021 data, respectively"]
- step 3: Derive 3D motion, projected distance and ages
  - method: Combine transverse and Doppler velocity for total velocity and orientation; age = distance/velocity from proper motion, no acceleration [Morphology and Ages of the ALMA Clumps: "The age estimates assume no acceleration or deceleration."]
  - assumption: Reference ejection epoch 2015 for ages [Morphology and Ages of the ALMA Clumps: "The reference epoch for the proper motions, 2015, is the reference date for when the clumps were ejected."]
  - validation: Acceleration effect 5-10%, less than age errors [Morphology and Ages of the ALMA Clumps: "showed that the effect was minimal, on the order of 5% to 10%"]
- result: Clump C proper motion = 3.7 ± 0.4 mas/yr [Table 2: "| Clump C | 320 | 122 | 23$\pm$2.0 | 3.7$\pm$0.4 | 20$\pm$2 | 102.0 $\pm$ 5 |"]
- result: Clump C transverse velocity = 20 ± 2 km/s [Table 2: "| Clump C | 320 | 122 | 23$\pm$2.0 | 3.7$\pm$0.4 | 20$\pm$2 | 102.0 $\pm$ 5 |"]
- result: Clump A transverse velocity = 46 ± 11 km/s [Table 2: "| Clump A | 560 | 19 | 53$\pm$12 | 8.5$\pm$2.0 | 46$\pm$11 | 27.5 $\pm$ 13 |"]
- result: Clump D transverse velocity = 52 ± 23 km/s [Table 2: "| Clump D | 716 | 120 | 59$\pm$25.3 | 9.5$\pm$4.1 | 52$\pm$23 | 138.3 $\pm$ 29 |"]
- result: Clump C age = 86 ± -7,+8 yr [Table 4: "| Clump C | 20$\pm$2 | +4$\pm$3 | 21$\pm$3 | +11$\pm$8 | 375$\pm$30 | 86$\pm$-7,+8 |"]
- result: Clump A age = 66 ± -12,+19 yr [Table 4: "| Clump A | 46$\pm$11 | -18$\pm$5 | 50$\pm$11 | -21$\pm$7 | 691$\pm$60 | 66$\pm$-12,+19 |"]
- limitation (authors): Clump B Doppler velocity very uncertain [Outflow Velocities of the Clumps: "We consider this to be very uncertain."]
- limitation (authors): Mass lower bounds for C and D; clumps poorly resolved [Mass Lost and the Mass Loss Mechanism: "The mass estimates, especially for Clumps C and D, are lower bounds"]
- not stated (card): Imaging parameters (tclean weighting, robust, deconvolver, cell size) given only in Paper I; CASA version; Initial Gaussian estimates for imfit; Dust opacity law and input parameters of the O'Gorman dust mass calculation; Peak-location algorithm for Figure 6 centroids; Renormalization procedure for continuum subtraction image; Line-free channel ranges and self-cal solution intervals

